+.Dd August 18, 2026
+.Dt LINUX_COMPAT_STUDY 7
+.Os
+.Sh NAME
+.Nm linux_compat_study
+.Nd rules for evaluating Linux kernel mechanisms in FreeBSD
+.Sh DESCRIPTION
+Linux may be used as a source of requirements, test cases, and architectural
+comparisons.
+Linux kernel source licensed under GPL must not be copied into the
+.Fx
+kernel.
+Implementations must use native interfaces and a licence suitable for the
+.Fx
+source tree.
+.Pp
+Before adding code, identify the existing native facility.
+Important mappings include:
+.Bl -tag -width "Linux cgroup v2"
+.It Linux RCU
+.Xr epoch 9
+and SMR.
+.It Linux cgroup v2 and namespaces
+RACCT, RCTL,
+.Xr jail 8 ,
+and VNET.
+.It Linux seccomp and Landlock
+Capsicum and the MAC Framework.
+.It Linux lockdep
+WITNESS and INVARIANTS.
+.It Linux ftrace and bootconfig
+DTrace, KTR, TSLOG, and boottrace.
+.It Linux fault injection
+.Xr fail 9 .
+.It Linux sendfile and kTLS
+The native
+.Xr sendfile 2
+and kernel TLS implementations.
+.It Linux sanitizers
+KASAN, KCSAN, KMSAN, and KCOV kernel configurations.
+.El
+.Sh DEVELOPMENT RULES
+A functional change requires a reproducible FreeBSD problem, a fixed source
+revision, tests, and measurements.
+Differences in design alone are not evidence that a port is useful.
+.Pp
+Prefer changes in this order:
+.Bl -enum
+.It
+Tests and observability using existing facilities.
+.It
+Userspace policy built on stable FreeBSD interfaces.
+.It
+Small native probes or counters with a demonstrated consumer.
+.It
+New kernel ABI or subsystem only after alternatives are exhausted.
+.El
+.Sh LABORATORY KERNELS
+Fault injection, coverage, sanitizers, TSLOG, WITNESS, and INVARIANTS may have
+security or performance cost.
+Destructive testing must use a separate kernel in a disposable virtual
+machine.
+A known-good GENERIC kernel must remain available for boot fallback.
+.Sh ACCEPTANCE
+A production patch must pass relevant ATF and KTest suites, buildworld,
+buildkernel, virtual-machine boot, security review, and before/after
+measurements.
+Rollback and licence provenance must be documented.
+.Sh SEE ALSO
+.Xr capsicum 4 ,
+.Xr dtrace 1 ,
+.Xr fail 9 ,
+.Xr jail 8 ,
+.Xr rctl 8 ,
+.Xr sendfile 2 ,
+.Xr tuning 7
